{"kind":"artifact","text":"Re-cut of 9197c43b onto main eb7d2dfd (after the 500k merge d6843b48 and the dead-helper cleanup cd375dc3). Part one of the kernel admission gaps: rests_on resolvability. internal/kernel refuses a submission whose rests_on carries a canonical event identifier for this log that names no position in it, with ErrUnresolvedReference naming the reference it could not resolve. A reference that makes no claim about this log - another workroom identifier, a URL, any other opaque string - is carried unchanged, so the kernel gains no application semantics. Resolution reads a commit index, Positions, maintained beside the dedup index on every path that builds one: cold scan, streamed delta, checkpoint restore (full and compact, retained and streamed), and local append; the check asks Git nothing. Verification and continuation read history exactly as before, so a dangling reference already in the log stays readable (TestVerifyAcceptsHistoricalDanglingReference). The carry differs from 9197c43b only where main renamed the checkpoint validators to their *Into forms with retainEvents: the Positions insert sits before the retain branch in validateCheckpointEventsInto, the compact reader and scanListedAfterMode, so streamed full reads that retain no Events still index every commit, and the streaming replay shares the base log's Positions map. Tests in internal/kernel/references_test.go: TestSubmitRefusesFabricatedInLogReference, TestSubmitterRefusesFabricatedInLogReference, TestSubmitAdmitsResolvedInLogReferences, TestSubmitRefusesSelfReference, TestSubmitRefusesCommitOutsideTheLog, TestSubmitCarriesReferencesItCannotResolve, TestVerifyAcceptsHistoricalDanglingReference. Mutation-checked at this head: disabling the Positions check fails the four refusal tests. Gates at this exact head: gofmt and go vet clean; go test -count=1 -race ./internal/kernel green; go test -count=1 ./... green in all 27 packages including the docset citation gate.","body":{"commit":"69f78d37210e4565bd59957b70f2f702f13c4d08","path":"internal/kernel"}}